B.aB9=new A.l9(B.md,"Who can see my bid?","Only you and the customer who posted the job. Other mechanics never see your price, and you never see theirs. The customer compares bids side by side and picks one.")
B.aB5=new A.l9(B.jE,"How do I size up a job before bidding?","Open the job and look at the description, the vehicle, and any photos or dealer quote the customer attached. If the customer has been rated by other mechanics, you'll see their star rating. Only bid on work you can do well \u2014 a bid is a promise to the customer.")
B.aB7=new A.l9(B.fP,"Why can't I see the customer's address or name right away?","It protects them, and it protects you. The service address unlocks only after you're chosen and the customer's payment is secured, so you never head out for a job that isn't paid for. A customer's other personal details stay private until you arrive.")
B.aBa=new A.l9(B.jF,"How and when do I get paid?","The customer's payment is secured before you start and held safely. When the work is done and the customer releases it, your share goes to your Stripe account. YCYC keeps 15% of the job price \u2014 no subscription, no fee for bidding.")
B.a0L=new A.ae(61640,"MaterialIcons",null,!1)
B.aBc=new A.l9(B.a0L,"What if I take a job outside the app?","Don't. Using YCYC to find a customer and then taking the job (or future jobs) off the app to skip the fee breaks your agreement. It can mean losing your account, paying back the fees, up to two times the original fee where the law allows, and legal action. Off the app you also lose payment protection: nothing guarantees you'll be paid.")
